          "id": "world-us-ai-chip-remote-access-rule-2026-11-16",
          "headline": "US tightens AI chip curbs to stop China using data centres abroad",
          "summary": "The US Commerce Department issued a rule on Monday to block Chinese firms from using remote access to advanced AI chips in data centres outside China. Shipping such chips to Singapore, Malaysia, Thailand, Indonesia and Brazil now needs a licence. The move follows the scandal around Singapore-based Megaspeed, now under a US criminal probe, that led Jensen Huang to quit as Nvidia CEO. Singapore says it is studying the rule.",
          "why_it_matters": "It hits chip sales and AI data-centre plans across Southeast Asia, just before Nvidia reports results.",
