          "headline": "FDA approves Roche's Wilserdly, an oral pill for ESR1-mutated breast cancer",
          "summary": "The FDA approved giredestrant (Wilserdly) from Roche's Genentech with everolimus for advanced ER-positive, HER2-negative breast cancer with an ESR1 mutation. In the evERA trial, patients with the mutation went a median 10 months without their cancer growing, against 5.5 months on standard treatment. A blood test, FoundationOne Liquid CDx, was approved to find eligible patients.",
          "why_it_matters": "It gives patients a new oral option, and Roche says it could become its top-selling drug.",
